## Deployment pipeline (local-first)

When asked to deploy, run **on the MacBook** in this order — do not skip verify:

```bash
vercel link --repo --yes --project 00-ulm
vercel pull --yes --environment=production
npm run verify          # typecheck + lint (same gate as CI)
vercel build --prod
vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod --force
```

- Project alignment: **`00-ulm`**. Production env pulls Neon secrets via `vercel pull`.
- Never push unverified assets; `vercel.json` build runs `npm run verify`.

## Master connection (env + cache reset)

Use to align local truth before postcode work. **DB reset is destructive** — dev/staging only, never production without explicit approval.

```bash
vercel pull --yes --environment=production && cp .vercel/.env.production.local .env.local
export $(grep -v '^#' .env.local | xargs) && psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "UPDATE cards SET visited = false, actioned = false;"
rm -rf .next
```

